James sought assistance in updating a methods appendix for a report on modeling catastrophic climate damages, initially calculated as expected losses using Howard and Sterner’s meta-analysis. The old method applied a deterministic adjustment based on a quadratic relationship, while the updated approach models stochastic events with a decay process to maintain the same expected losses. The revised method introduces individual catastrophic events with a defined loss size (25% of GDP) and includes parameters for event probability and decay rate. Outcomes from Monte Carlo simulations produce a dataset of losses over time, allowing for the construction of summary indicators. The final output includes LaTeX figures illustrating simulated damages and expected losses, demonstrating the model's structure and results.
